                '  <p>Once completed, log into your WHM dashboard and search for <strong>LiteSpeed Web Server '
                'Plugin</strong> under the Plugins section.</p>\n'
                '</section>\n'
                '\n'
                '<section class="space-y-4">\n'
                '  <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-navy">Step 2: Installing LiteSpeed '
                'Web Server via WHM</h2>\n'
                '  <p>Inside the LiteSpeed WHM Plugin interface:</p>\n'
                '  <ol class="list-decimal space-y-2 pl-6 text-gray-700">\n'
                '    <li>Click <strong>Install LiteSpeed Web Server</strong>.</li>\n'
                '    <li>Select <em>I agree to the license agreement</em> and choose your license source (LicenBase '
                'automated IP license).</li>\n'
                '    <li>Set port offset to <code>0</code> for direct replacement, or <code>2000</code> if you wish to '
                'test on alternate ports first.</li>\n'
                '    <li>Enter your administrator email address and proceed with the installation.</li>\n'
                '  </ol>\n'
                '</section>\n'
                '\n'
                '<section class="space-y-4">\n'
                '  <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-navy">Step 3: Building Matching PHP '
                '(lsphp) Modules</h2>\n'
                '  <p>To ensure all existing PHP extensions match your EasyApache 4 profile, click <strong>Build '
                'Matching PHP</strong> inside the LiteSpeed plugin. The compiler matches all installed PHP modules '
                '(GD, cURL, imagick, ionCube) into optimized <code>lsphp</code> binaries automatically.</p>\n'
                '</section>\n'
                '\n'
                '<section class="space-y-4">\n'
                '  <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-navy">Step 4: Switching from Apache '
                'to LiteSpeed</h2>\n'
                '  <p>Once PHP compilation completes:</p>\n'
                '  <ol class="list-decimal space-y-2 pl-6 text-gray-700">\n'
                '    <li>Click <strong>Switch to LiteSpeed</strong> in the WHM plugin.</li>\n'
