                '1024M for memory-intensive WooCommerce checkouts.</li>\n'
                '    <li><strong>Keep-Alive Timeout:</strong> Lower to 5 seconds to free idle TCP connections '
                'quickly.</li>\n'
                '  </ul>\n'
                '</section>\n'
                '\n'
                '<section class="space-y-4">\n'
                '  <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-navy">Configuring Object Caching '
                'with Redis</h2>\n'
                '  <p>For dynamic database caching on high-traffic WooCommerce and forum communities, pair LiteSpeed '
                'with a localized Redis service:</p>\n'
                '  <pre class="overflow-x-auto rounded-xl bg-navy p-4 text-sm leading-relaxed text-gray-100"><code>dnf '
                'install -y redis &amp;&amp; systemctl enable --now redis</code></pre>\n'
                '  <p>Enable the Redis Object Cache integration directly inside the WordPress LSCache settings under '
                '<em>Cache > [6] Object</em>, pointing to <code>127.0.0.1:6379</code>. This reduces database query '
                'load by up to 90%.</p>\n'
                '</section>\n'
                '\n'
                '<section class="space-y-4">\n'
                '  <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-navy">Verifying HTTP/3 QUIC and '
                'Cache Headers</h2>\n'
                '  <p>To confirm LiteSpeed is serving traffic with full caching and QUIC acceleration, run a cURL '
                'check against any hosted domain:</p>\n'
                '  <pre class="overflow-x-auto rounded-xl bg-navy p-4 text-sm leading-relaxed '
                'text-gray-100"><code>curl -I https://yourdomain.com</code></pre>\n'
                '  <p>Look for the <code>server: LiteSpeed</code> and <code>x-litespeed-cache: hit</code> response '
                'headers. If present, your server is operating at peak performance.</p>\n'
                '</section>\n',
