                '<p class="text-lg text-gray-600">Deploying a new Linux Virtual Private Server (VPS) takes only '
                'seconds, but deploying websites on an unhardened server invites immediate brute-force scans, malware '
                'injection, and unauthorized intrusion. Before configuring domains or installing a control panel, '
                'executing a systematic security hardening routine is mandatory. Here is the essential step-by-step '
                'security checklist for any production Linux VPS.</p>\n'
                '\n'
                '<section class="space-y-4">\n'
                '  <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-navy">1. SSH Hardening: Keys and '
                'Non-Default Ports</h2>\n'
                '  <p>SSH is the primary target of automated credential stuffing. Harden SSH configuration in '
                '<code>/etc/ssh/sshd_config</code>:</p>\n'
                '  <figure class="my-2"><img src="/assets/img/blog/secure-linux-vps-hosting-websites-1.svg" alt="Linux '
                'VPS hardening and multi-layer security stack" width="960" height="420" loading="lazy" '
                'decoding="async" class="w-full rounded-2xl border border-gray-200" /><figcaption class="mt-2 '
                'text-center text-xs text-gray-500">Multi-layer security architecture: SSH hardening, firewalls, '
                'kernel isolation, and AI WAF.</figcaption></figure>\n'
                '  <ul class="list-disc space-y-2 pl-6">\n'
                '    <li><strong>Create a Sudo User:</strong> Create a non-root administrator account: <code>adduser '
                'adminuser &amp;&amp; usermod -aG wheel adminuser</code>.</li>\n'
                '    <li><strong>Deploy Ed25519 SSH Keys:</strong> Copy your public key to '
                '<code>~/.ssh/authorized_keys</code> and disable password login.</li>\n'
                '    <li><strong>Disable Root Password Login:</strong> Set <code>PermitRootLogin '
                'prohibit-password</code> and <code>PasswordAuthentication no</code>.</li>\n'
                '    <li><strong>Change the SSH Port:</strong> Change port 22 to a custom high port (e.g. <code>Port '
                '22220</code>) to filter 99% of automated mass scanners.</li>\n'
                '  </ul>\n'
                '</section>\n'
                '\n'
                '<section class="space-y-4">\n'
                '  <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-navy">2. Firewall and Intrusion '
                'Prevention</h2>\n'
                '  <p>Never expose unneeded ports to the public internet. Deploy a robust firewall and intrusion '
                'prevention system:</p>\n'
                '  <ul class="list-disc space-y-2 pl-6">\n'
                '    <li><strong>Configure UFW or CSF:</strong> Restrict open inbound ports strictly to HTTP (80), '
                'HTTPS (443), DNS (53), and your custom SSH port.</li>\n'
                '    <li><strong>Install Fail2ban:</strong> Monitor system authentication logs and automatically ban '
                'IP addresses after 3 failed login attempts.</li>\n'
                '    <li><strong>Enable SYN Flood Protection:</strong> Tune TCP stack parameters in '
                '<code>/etc/sysctl.conf</code> (e.g. <code>net.ipv4.tcp_syncookies = 1</code>).</li>\n'
                '  </ul>\n'
                '</section>\n'
                '\n'
                '<section class="space-y-4">\n'
                '  <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-navy">3. Partition Hardening and '
                'Kernel Protections</h2>\n'
                '  <p>Secure vulnerable shared memory directories where attackers typically attempt to compile '
                'unauthorized binaries:</p>\n'
                '  <pre class="overflow-x-auto rounded-xl bg-navy p-4 text-sm leading-relaxed text-gray-100"><code># '
                'Add to /etc/fstab\n'
                'tmpfs /tmp tmpfs defaults,noexec,nosuid,nodev 0 0\n'
                'tmpfs /var/tmp tmpfs defaults,noexec,nosuid,nodev 0 0</code></pre>\n'
                '  <p>Enable automatic security updates so critical kernel and package vulnerabilities patch '
                'automatically without manual intervention.</p>\n'
                '</section>\n'
                '\n'
                '<section class="space-y-4">\n'
                '  <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-navy">4. Multi-Tenant Kernel '
                'Isolation with CloudLinux</h2>\n'
                '  <p>If you plan to host multiple client websites or resell hosting packages, operating system '
                'virtualization is essential. Deploying <a href="/cloudlinux-license" class="font-semibold text-brand '
                'hover:underline">CloudLinux OS</a> converts your standard Linux kernel into a multi-tenant '
                'bastion:</p>\n'
                '  <ul class="list-disc space-y-2 pl-6">\n'
