                'and Why Are They Lethal for Servers?</h2>\n'
                '  <p>Nulled software refers to commercial software that has been reverse-engineered and patched to '
                'bypass license verification checks. In the server hosting industry, running nulled control panels '
                'introduces severe risks:</p>\n'
                '  <ul class="list-disc space-y-2 pl-6">\n'
                '    <li><strong>Malicious Code Injection:</strong> Creators of cracked scripts insert hidden PHP web '
                'shells, rootkit droppers, and outbound DDoS botnet daemons.</li>\n'
                '    <li><strong>Frozen Security Updates:</strong> Because cracked scripts tamper with binary files, '
                'running official system updates (<code>dnf update</code> or <code>upcp</code>) breaks the crack and '
                'bricks the WHM interface.</li>\n'
                '    <li><strong>Zero Day Vulnerabilities:</strong> Without upstream security patches, your server '
                'remains vulnerable to known exploits that allow remote code execution.</li>\n'
                '    <li><strong>IP Blacklisting:</strong> Rogue outbound spam and malware traffic will quickly get '
                "your server's IP blacklisted by Spamhaus, Google Safe Browsing, and Microsoft SNDS.</li>\n"
                '  </ul>\n'
                '</section>\n'
