                '<p class="text-lg text-gray-600">When setting up a shared or reseller web hosting server, '
                'administrators must choose between standard free enterprise Linux distributions (such as AlmaLinux, '
                'Rocky Linux, or Ubuntu) and a commercial operating system like CloudLinux OS. With a typical retail '
                'licensing cost of $16 to $22+ per month per server, founders and system engineers often question: is '
                'the extra cost of a CloudLinux license genuinely worth it? In this technical and financial '
                'evaluation, we explain why CloudLinux is considered essential infrastructure for professional web '
                'hosting providers.</p>\n'
                '\n'
                '<section class="space-y-4">\n'
                '  <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-navy">The Shared Hosting \'Bad '
                "Neighbor' Problem</h2>\n"
                '  <p>On a vanilla Linux server running standard Apache and cPanel, all hosting accounts share the '
                'same global resource pool. This architectural limitation creates significant operational risks:</p>\n'
                '  <figure class="my-2"><img '
                'src="/assets/img/blog/cloudlinux-license-web-hosting-worth-the-cost-1.svg" alt="CloudLinux OS '
                'architecture comparison diagram showing CageFS isolation and LVE resource limits" width="960" '
                'height="420" loading="lazy" decoding="async" class="w-full rounded-2xl border border-gray-200" '
                '/><figcaption class="mt-2 text-center text-xs text-gray-500">Comparison between standard shared Linux '
                'architecture and CloudLinux LVE tenant isolation.</figcaption></figure>\n'
                '  <ul class="list-disc space-y-2 pl-6">\n'
                '    <li><strong>CPU &amp; RAM Hijacking:</strong> A single compromised WordPress site or runaway '
                'script can consume 100% of server CPU and RAM, slowing down or crashing all other tenant websites on '
                'the machine.</li>\n'
                '    <li><strong>Cross-Account Information Leaks:</strong> Standard Linux permissions can allow '
                'malicious scripts to read `/etc/passwd` or inspect directory paths belonging to adjacent users.</li>\n'
                '    <li><strong>MySQL Database Saturation:</strong> A poorly indexed database query from one user can '
                'exhaust MySQL connection limits, triggering database downtime across the entire server fleet.</li>\n'
                '  </ul>\n'
                '</section>\n'
                '\n'
                '<section class="space-y-4">\n'
                '  <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-navy">How CloudLinux Solves Server '
                'Instability</h2>\n'
                '  <p>CloudLinux replaces standard kernel scheduling with enterprise-grade multi-tenant isolation '
                'technologies:</p>\n'
                '  <ul class="list-disc space-y-2 pl-6">\n'
                '    <li><strong>Lightweight Virtual Environments (LVE):</strong> Sets hard CPU, memory, IOPS, and '
                'entry process limits on a per-user basis. If one site experiences a traffic spike, only that specific '
                'user is throttled without impacting neighboring clients.</li>\n'
                '    <li><strong>CageFS Virtualized File System:</strong> Encloses each user inside a secure virtual '
                'container, preventing them from viewing other users, server config files, or processes.</li>\n'
                '    <li><strong>MySQL Governor:</strong> Automatically throttles abusive database queries in '
                'real-time, preventing database service crashes.</li>\n'
                '    <li><strong>Hardened PHP &amp; PHP Selector:</strong> Gives clients the ability to choose '
                'individual PHP versions (from 5.6 to 8.3+) while patching legacy PHP security vulnerabilities '
                'automatically.</li>\n'
                '  </ul>\n'
                '</section>\n'
                '\n'
                '<section class="space-y-4">\n'
                '  <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-navy">Financial ROI: How CloudLinux '
                'Multiplies Hosting Density</h2>\n'
                '  <p>While CloudLinux adds a modest monthly software fee, it dramatically improves server density and '
                'hardware return on investment:</p>\n'
                '  <div class="overflow-x-auto rounded-xl border border-gray-200"><table class="w-full min-w-[34rem] '
                'text-sm"><thead><tr><th class="border-b border-gray-200 bg-mist px-4 py-3 text-left text-xs font-bold '
                'uppercase tracking-wider text-gray-600">Metric</th><th class="border-b border-gray-200 bg-mist px-4 '
                'py-3 text-left text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-gray-600">Standard Free Linux '
                'Server</th><th class="border-b border-gray-200 bg-mist px-4 py-3 text-left text-xs font-bold '
                'uppercase tracking-wider text-gray-600">CloudLinux OS Server</th><th class="border-b border-gray-200 '
                'bg-mist px-4 py-3 text-left text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-gray-600">Business '
                'Advantage</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class="border-b border-gray-100 px-4 py-3 align-top">Safe '
