                '<p class="text-lg text-gray-600">A full disk drive on a Linux Virtual Private Server is an urgent '
                'operational emergency. When storage reaches 100% utilization, databases lock up, email mailboxes stop '
                'receiving messages, cron jobs fail, and web applications crash due to session write errors. Locating '
                'and purging unneeded log archives, orphaned backup files, package caches, and temporary directories '
                'quickly restores healthy filesystem capacity. Follow these 12 proven methods to reclaim gigabytes of '
                'storage safely.</p>\n'
                '\n'
                '<section class="space-y-4">\n'
                '  <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-navy">12-Step VPS Disk Reclamation '
                'Hierarchy</h2>\n'
                '  <p>Safely freeing disk storage requires systematically inspecting system journal logs, package '
                'repositories, database binary logs, and user home directories.</p>\n'
                '  <figure class="my-2"><img src="/assets/img/blog/vps-disk-space-full-cleanup-guide-1.svg" alt="12 '
                'practical methods to find, clean, and reclaim storage on a full Linux VPS server" width="960" '
                'height="420" loading="lazy" decoding="async" class="w-full rounded-2xl border border-gray-200" '
                '/><figcaption class="mt-2 text-center text-xs text-gray-500">Hierarchy of disk space cleanup actions '
                'for Linux virtual servers.</figcaption></figure>\n'
                '  <p>Working through this hierarchy ensures you clean disposable temporary caches first before '
                'touching user files or application databases.</p>\n'
                '</section>\n'
                '\n'
                '<section class="space-y-4">\n'
                '  <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-navy">12 Ways to Find and Remove '
                'Storage Bloat</h2>\n'
                '  <ol class="list-disc space-y-2 pl-6">\n'
                '    <li><strong>1. Vacuum Systemd Journal Logs:</strong> Limit systemd journal logs to a maximum of '
                '200 MB:\n'
                '      <div class="overflow-x-auto rounded-xl bg-navy p-4 text-sm leading-relaxed '
                'text-gray-100"><pre><code>journalctl --vacuum-size=200M</code></pre></div>\n'
                '    </li>\n'
                '    <li><strong>2. Clean Package Manager Caches:</strong> Remove downloaded RPM/DEB package cache '
                'files:\n'
                '      <div class="overflow-x-auto rounded-xl bg-navy p-4 text-sm leading-relaxed '
                'text-gray-100"><pre><code># AlmaLinux / RHEL / Rocky Linux\n'
                'dnf clean all &amp;&amp; rm -rf /var/cache/dnf\n'
                '\n'
                '# Ubuntu / Debian\n'
                'apt clean &amp;&amp; apt autoremove -y</code></pre></div>\n'
                '    </li>\n'
                '    <li><strong>3. Purge MySQL / MariaDB Binary Logs:</strong> If binary logging is enabled, purge '
                'expired logs older than 3 days inside MySQL:\n'
                '      <div class="overflow-x-auto rounded-xl bg-navy p-4 text-sm leading-relaxed '
                'text-gray-100"><pre><code>PURGE BINARY LOGS BEFORE NOW() - INTERVAL 3 DAY;</code></pre></div>\n'
                '    </li>\n'
                '    <li><strong>4. Find and Remove Files Larger Than 100 MB:</strong> Search the filesystem for giant '
                'files:\n'
                '      <div class="overflow-x-auto rounded-xl bg-navy p-4 text-sm leading-relaxed '
                'text-gray-100"><pre><code>find / -type f -size +100M -exec ls -lh {} \\; | awk \'{ print $9 ": " $5 '
                "}'</code></pre></div>\n"
                '    </li>\n'
                '    <li><strong>5. Clear Stale Temporary Files in /tmp and /var/tmp:</strong> Remove abandoned upload '
                'sessions:\n'
                '      <div class="overflow-x-auto rounded-xl bg-navy p-4 text-sm leading-relaxed '
                'text-gray-100"><pre><code>rm -rf /tmp/* /var/tmp/*</code></pre></div>\n'
                '    </li>\n'
                '    <li><strong>6. Empty cPanel Trash Directories:</strong> Users often delete files via File Manager '
                'without realizing they sit in <code class="rounded bg-mist px-1.5 py-0.5 text-[0.85em] '
                'text-navy">.trash</code> folders:\n'
                '      <div class="overflow-x-auto rounded-xl bg-navy p-4 text-sm leading-relaxed '
                'text-gray-100"><pre><code>rm -rf /home/*/.trash/*</code></pre></div>\n'
                '    </li>\n'
                '    <li><strong>7. Locate Orphaned cPanel Backup Archives:</strong> Search user directories for '
                'forgotten manual backups:\n'
                '      <div class="overflow-x-auto rounded-xl bg-navy p-4 text-sm leading-relaxed '
                'text-gray-100"><pre><code>find /home -name "backup-*.tar.gz" -type f -delete</code></pre></div>\n'
                '    </li>\n'
                '    <li><strong>8. Release Deleted Files Held Open by Processes:</strong> Free disk space held by '
                'running processes:\n'
                '      <div class="overflow-x-auto rounded-xl bg-navy p-4 text-sm leading-relaxed '
                'text-gray-100"><pre><code>lsof | grep deleted</code></pre></div>\n'
                '      <p>Restart the corresponding service to release the unlinked disk blocks.</p>\n'
                '    </li>\n'
                '    <li><strong>9. Truncate Overgrown Web Server Access Logs:</strong> Rotate or truncate huge logs '
                'in <code class="rounded bg-mist px-1.5 py-0.5 text-[0.85em] text-navy">/var/log/httpd</code> or <code '
                'class="rounded bg-mist px-1.5 py-0.5 text-[0.85em] text-navy">/var/log/nginx</code>.</li>\n'
                '    <li><strong>10. Remove Old Kernel Images:</strong> On Ubuntu/Debian, purge unused old kernels '
                'with <code class="rounded bg-mist px-1.5 py-0.5 text-[0.85em] text-navy">apt --purge '
                'autoremove</code>.</li>\n'
                '    <li><strong>11. Empty Spam and Mail Queues:</strong> Clear undeliverable exim/postfix mail queues '
                'if the server was subjected to email bounces.</li>\n'
                '    <li><strong>12. Switch to Offsite Cloud Backups:</strong> Replace heavy local backup routines '
                'with a <a href="/jetbackup-license" class="font-semibold text-brand hover:underline">JetBackup '
                'license</a> that streams snapshots directly to Wasabi or Amazon S3.</li>\n'
                '  </ol>\n'
                '</section>\n'
