                '<p class="text-lg text-gray-600">A virtual private server pinned at 100% CPU usage is an immediate '
                'operational emergency. When CPU capacity is exhausted, web requests queue indefinitely, SSH sessions '
                'become sluggish or freeze, database queries time out, and automated cron jobs fail. Diagnosing the '
                'underlying cause requires a structured triage methodology. In this guide, we walk through 15 '
                'actionable ways to isolate runaway processes, optimize web runtimes, tune database engines, and '
                'permanently stabilize your Linux VPS performance.</p>\n'
                '\n'
                '<section class="space-y-4">\n'
                '  <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-navy">1. Live Process Triage with '
                'Top, Htop, and Pidstat</h2>\n'
                '  <p>The first step during a CPU spike is establishing whether user space applications, kernel system '
                'calls, or software interrupts are consuming compute cycles. Connect to your VPS via SSH and run <code '
                'class="rounded bg-mist px-1.5 py-0.5 text-[0.85em] text-navy">top</code> or <code class="rounded '
                'bg-mist px-1.5 py-0.5 text-[0.85em] text-navy">htop</code>:</p>\n'
                '  <pre class="overflow-x-auto rounded-xl bg-navy p-4 text-sm leading-relaxed text-gray-100"><code># '
                'Launch top and sort by CPU usage\n'
                'top -b -n 1 | head -n 20\n'
                '\n'
                '# Run pidstat to sample process CPU utilization over 5 seconds\n'
                'pidstat -u 1 5</code></pre>\n'
                '  <p>Pay close attention to the CPU summary line in <code class="rounded bg-mist px-1.5 py-0.5 '
                'text-[0.85em] text-navy">top</code>:</p>\n'
                '  <ul class="list-disc space-y-2 pl-6">\n'
                '    <li><strong>%us (User Time):</strong> Indicates applications like PHP-FPM, Python, Node.js, or '
                'MariaDB are executing intensive computation.</li>\n'
                '    <li><strong>%sy (System Time):</strong> Indicates kernel overhead, excessive context switching, '
                'or memory allocation contention.</li>\n'
                '    <li><strong>%wa (I/O Wait):</strong> Indicates the CPU is waiting on slow disk storage or swap '
                'thrashing rather than pure computing bottlenecks.</li>\n'
                '    <li><strong>%si (Software Interrupts):</strong> Points toward heavy network packet processing, '
                'often seen during Layer 7 DDoS attacks.</li>\n'
                '  </ul>\n'
                '  <figure class="my-2"><img src="/assets/img/blog/vps-cpu-100-percent-15-ways-find-fix-1.svg" '
                'alt="Linux VPS 100 percent CPU troubleshooting and fixes workflow" width="960" height="420" '
                'loading="lazy" decoding="async" class="w-full rounded-2xl border border-gray-200" /><figcaption '
                'class="mt-2 text-center text-xs text-gray-500">Four-stage process to isolate runaway processes, '
                'optimize runtimes, and enforce tenant limits.</figcaption></figure>\n'
                '</section>\n'
                '\n'
                '<section class="space-y-4">\n'
                '  <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-navy">2. Detecting and Killing Rogue '
                'Runaway Processes</h2>\n'
                '  <p>If a specific script or background worker is stuck in an infinite loop, identify its Process ID '
                '(PID) and inspect its open file descriptors before terminating it:</p>\n'
                '  <pre class="overflow-x-auto rounded-xl bg-navy p-4 text-sm leading-relaxed text-gray-100"><code># '
                'Find the top 5 CPU-consuming processes with exact command paths\n'
                'ps -eo pid,ppid,cmd,%mem,%cpu --sort=-%cpu | head -n 6\n'
                '\n'
                '# Inspect files and sockets held by the runaway PID\n'
                'lsof -p &lt;PID&gt;\n'
                '\n'
                '# Gracefully terminate the process, then force kill if unresponsive\n'
                'kill -15 &lt;PID&gt;\n'
                'kill -9 &lt;PID&gt;</code></pre>\n'
                '  <p>If recurring runaway processes originate from user web directories, check for malicious '
                'obfuscated PHP shell scripts in <code class="rounded bg-mist px-1.5 py-0.5 text-[0.85em] '
                'text-navy">/tmp</code> or <code class="rounded bg-mist px-1.5 py-0.5 text-[0.85em] '
                'text-navy">/dev/shm</code>. Adding an <a href="/imunify360-license" class="font-semibold text-brand '
                'hover:underline">Imunify360 license</a> provides real-time automated malware scanning and background '
                'script behavioral quarantine.</p>\n'
                '</section>\n'
                '\n'
                '<section class="space-y-4">\n'
                '  <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-navy">3. Tuning PHP-FPM Worker Pools '
                'and Process Managers</h2>\n'
                '  <p>Misconfigured PHP-FPM pool directives frequently trigger massive CPU exhaustion when traffic '
                'surges. If your pool is set to dynamic with excessive <code class="rounded bg-mist px-1.5 py-0.5 '
                'text-[0.85em] text-navy">pm.max_children</code>, hundreds of concurrent PHP workers will compete for '
                'CPU cache and memory:</p>\n'
                '  <div class="overflow-x-auto rounded-xl border border-gray-200"><table class="w-full min-w-[34rem] '
                'text-sm"><thead><tr><th class="border-b border-gray-200 bg-mist px-4 py-3 text-left text-xs font-bold '
                'uppercase tracking-wider text-gray-600">PHP-FPM Directive</th><th class="border-b border-gray-200 '
                'bg-mist px-4 py-3 text-left text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-gray-600">Default / Risky '
                'Setting</th><th class="border-b border-gray-200 bg-mist px-4 py-3 text-left text-xs font-bold '
                'uppercase tracking-wider text-gray-600">Optimized Production Setting</th><th class="border-b '
                'border-gray-200 bg-mist px-4 py-3 text-left text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider '
                'text-gray-600">Impact on CPU</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class="border-b border-gray-100 px-4 '
                'py-3 align-top">pm (Process Manager)</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 px-4 py-3 '
                'align-top">dynamic</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 px-4 py-3 align-top">ondemand</td><td '
                'class="border-b border-gray-100 px-4 py-3 align-top">Spawns workers strictly when requests arrive; '
                'terminates idle workers.</td></tr><tr><td class="border-b border-gray-100 px-4 py-3 '
                'align-top">pm.max_children</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 px-4 py-3 align-top">50 - 100 '
                '(Unbounded)</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 px-4 py-3 align-top">Calculated by RAM / '
                '45MB</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 px-4 py-3 align-top">Prevents process storming and CPU '
                'core thrashing.</td></tr><tr><td class="border-b border-gray-100 px-4 py-3 '
                'align-top">pm.process_idle_timeout</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 px-4 py-3 '
                'align-top">10s</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 px-4 py-3 align-top">10s - 15s</td><td '
                'class="border-b border-gray-100 px-4 py-3 align-top">Quickly frees compute memory once web traffic '
                'bursts subside.</td></tr><tr><td class="border-b border-gray-100 px-4 py-3 '
                'align-top">pm.max_requests</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 px-4 py-3 align-top">0 '
                '(Unlimited)</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 px-4 py-3 align-top">500 - 1000</td><td '
                'class="border-b border-gray-100 px-4 py-3 align-top">Recycles worker processes to eliminate '
                'progressive memory leaks.</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n'
                '  <p>Configure your PHP-FPM pool configuration file (located in <code class="rounded bg-mist px-1.5 '
                'py-0.5 text-[0.85em] text-navy">/etc/php-fpm.d/www.conf</code> on AlmaLinux/cPanel or <code '
                'class="rounded bg-mist px-1.5 py-0.5 text-[0.85em] text-navy">/etc/php/8.x/fpm/pool.d/www.conf</code> '
                'on Ubuntu) to use ondemand mode for efficient CPU scaling.</p>\n'
                '</section>\n'
                '\n'
                '<section class="space-y-4">\n'
                '  <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-navy">4. Finding and Optimizing '
                'MySQL / MariaDB Slow Queries</h2>\n'
                '  <p>Unindexed database tables and complex JOIN operations can instantly lock CPU cores at 100%. '
                'Enable the MySQL slow query log to capture unoptimized queries:</p>\n'
                '  <pre class="overflow-x-auto rounded-xl bg-navy p-4 text-sm leading-relaxed text-gray-100"><code># '
                'Enable slow query logging in my.cnf\n'
                '[mysqld]\n'
                'slow_query_log = 1\n'
                'slow_query_log_file = /var/log/mysql/slow-query.log\n'
                'long_query_time = 1\n'
                'log_queries_not_using_indexes = 1\n'
                '\n'
                '# Check currently running database threads in real time\n'
                'mysqladmin processlist -u root -p</code></pre>\n'
                '  <p>If you see queries stuck in "Copying to tmp table" or "Sorting result", analyze the table '
                'structure with <code class="rounded bg-mist px-1.5 py-0.5 text-[0.85em] text-navy">EXPLAIN '
                '&lt;query&gt;</code> and add composite indexes to eliminate full table scans. Make sure your <code '
                'class="rounded bg-mist px-1.5 py-0.5 text-[0.85em] text-navy">innodb_buffer_pool_size</code> is set '
                'to roughly 50% to 70% of available server RAM to prevent disk I/O CPU stalls.</p>\n'
                '</section>\n'
                '\n'
                '<section class="space-y-4">\n'
                '  <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-navy">5. Upgrading from Apache to '
                'LiteSpeed Web Server</h2>\n'
                '  <p>Apache using traditional MPM prefork or worker architectures allocates heavy process threads for '
                'every keep-alive connection. Under traffic spikes or Layer 7 crawl floods, Apache threads overwhelm '
                'VPS CPU capacity.</p>\n'
                '  <p>Replacing Apache with an official <a href="/litespeed-license" class="font-semibold text-brand '
                'hover:underline">LiteSpeed license</a> eliminates this bottleneck. LiteSpeed features an event-driven '
                'core capable of serving static assets and cached dynamic pages with negligible CPU usage. Combined '
                'with server-side LSCache, LiteSpeed bypasses PHP-FPM execution entirely for up to 95% of incoming '
                'page requests, dropping total server CPU load dramatically.</p>\n'
                '</section>\n'
                '\n'
                '<section class="space-y-4">\n'
                '  <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-navy">6. Mitigating Malicious Bot '
                'Crawlers and Layer 7 Attacks</h2>\n'
                '  <p>Scraper bots, automated vulnerability scanners, and brute-force login attempts against <code '
                'class="rounded bg-mist px-1.5 py-0.5 text-[0.85em] text-navy">wp-login.php</code> or <code '
                'class="rounded bg-mist px-1.5 py-0.5 text-[0.85em] text-navy">xmlrpc.php</code> can consume all CPU '
                'threads without generating legitimate traffic:</p>\n'
                '  <ul class="list-disc space-y-2 pl-6">\n'
                '    <li><strong>Block Abusive User Agents:</strong> Add Nginx or LiteSpeed rewrite rules to reject '
                'empty, scrapers, and malicious bot user agents.</li>\n'
                '    <li><strong>Enforce Rate Limiting:</strong> Use Fail2ban or Cloudflare WAF rate-limiting rules to '
                'restrict excessive requests per IP.</li>\n'
                '    <li><strong>Disable XML-RPC:</strong> Block XML-RPC endpoints in WordPress to stop distributed '
                'brute-force amplification attacks.</li>\n'
                '  </ul>\n'
                '</section>\n'
                '\n'
                '<section class="space-y-4">\n'
                '  <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-navy">7. Enforcing Multi-Tenant '
                'Isolation with CloudLinux OS</h2>\n'
                '  <p>On multi-user hosting servers managed with <a href="/cpanel-license" class="font-semibold '
                'text-brand hover:underline">cPanel &amp; WHM</a> or <a href="/plesk-license" class="font-semibold '
                'text-brand hover:underline">Plesk</a>, a single customer site can exhaust the entire VPS CPU pool, '
                'causing downtime for all other hosted accounts.</p>\n'
                '  <p>Deploying a <a href="/cloudlinux-license" class="font-semibold text-brand '
                'hover:underline">CloudLinux license</a> solves this with kernel-level Lightweight Virtual '
                'Environments (LVE). You can set strict per-user CPU limits (e.g. 100% of 1 core max), memory bounds, '
                'and concurrent I/O throttles. If one website experiences a traffic spike or infinite loop, CloudLinux '
                'isolates the process, returning a temporary 508 Resource Limit Reached error to that specific site '
                'while the rest of your server continues running smoothly. Explore our <a href="/deals" '
                'class="font-semibold text-brand hover:underline">combo discount stacks</a> to bundle cPanel, '
                'CloudLinux, and LiteSpeed for enterprise server stability.</p>\n'
                '</section>\n',
