                '<p class="text-lg text-gray-600">Activating a cPanel &amp; WHM license on a Linux Virtual Private '
                'Server (VPS) is a quick, straightforward process when using automated IP licensing. Whether you are '
                'provisioning a fresh server from scratch or reactivating an expired trial installation, this '
                'comprehensive step-by-step tutorial will have your WHM root administration console 100% unlocked and '
                'functional in under two minutes.</p>\n'
                '\n'
                '<section class="space-y-4">\n'
                '  <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-navy">1. The 3-Step Automated '
                'Activation Workflow</h2>\n'
                '  <p>The activation flow consists of three seamless phases:</p>\n'
                '  <figure class="my-2"><img src="/assets/img/blog/how-to-activate-cpanel-license-on-vps-1.svg" '
                'alt="3-step automated activation flow for cPanel license on a VPS" width="960" height="420" '
                'loading="lazy" decoding="async" class="w-full rounded-2xl border border-gray-200" /><figcaption '
                'class="mt-2 text-center text-xs text-gray-500">Step-by-step cPanel license activation flow on '
                'VPS.</figcaption></figure>\n'
                "  <p>Because verification binds directly to your server's public IPv4 address, there is no need to "
                'enter complicated alphanumeric license keys or upload license certificate files.</p>\n'
                '</section>\n'
                '\n'
                '<section class="space-y-4">\n'
                '  <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-navy">2. Step 1: Obtain and Bind '
                'Your Server Public IP</h2>\n'
                '  <p>Connect to your VPS via SSH and retrieve your public IPv4 address:</p>\n'
                '  <pre class="overflow-x-auto rounded-xl bg-navy p-4 text-sm leading-relaxed text-gray-100"><code># '
                'Display public IPv4 address:\n'
                'curl -4 icanhazip.com</code></pre>\n'
                '  <p>Navigate to the <a href="/cpanel-license" class="font-semibold text-brand '
                'hover:underline">LicenBase cPanel License page</a>, select the VPS Tier ($4.00/month), and enter your '
                'public IPv4 address during checkout. The license provisions automatically in our high-availability '
                'authentication cluster upon payment completion.</p>\n'
                '</section>\n'
                '\n'
                '<section class="space-y-4">\n'
                '  <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-navy">3. Step 2: Execute the 1-Line '
                'Activation Script</h2>\n'
                '  <p>In your VPS SSH terminal, execute the official LicenBase activation command as root:</p>\n'
                '  <pre class="overflow-x-auto rounded-xl bg-navy p-4 text-sm leading-relaxed text-gray-100"><code># '
                'Run as root in your server terminal:\n'
                "curl -fsSL 'https://verify.licenbase.com/install/cpanel' | bash</code></pre>\n"
                '  <p>The script performs the following automated actions:</p>\n'
                '  <ul class="list-disc space-y-2 pl-6">\n'
                "    <li>Validates your server's public IPv4 address with the LicenBase verification network.</li>\n"
                '    <li>Sets up high-availability failover endpoints for uninterrupted authentication.</li>\n'
                '    <li>Executes <code class="rounded bg-mist px-1.5 py-0.5 text-[0.85em] text-navy">cpkeyclt</code> '
                'to synchronize local license keys with the cPanel daemon.</li>\n'
                '    <li>Installs the <code class="rounded bg-mist px-1.5 py-0.5 text-[0.85em] '
                'text-navy">licenbase_cpanel</code> CLI utility for quick future diagnostics.</li>\n'
                '  </ul>\n'
                '</section>\n'
                '\n'
                '<section class="space-y-4">\n'
                '  <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-navy">4. Step 3: Verify Active '
                'Licensing and Log In to WHM</h2>\n'
                '  <p>Verify that your license is active using either command:</p>\n'
                '  <pre class="overflow-x-auto rounded-xl bg-navy p-4 text-sm leading-relaxed text-gray-100"><code># '
                'Verify with LicenBase CLI:\n'
                'licenbase_cpanel\n'
                '\n'
                '# Or check with official cPanel key client:\n'
                '/usr/local/cpanel/cpkeyclt</code></pre>\n'
                '  <p>Once you see <code class="rounded bg-mist px-1.5 py-0.5 text-[0.85em] text-navy">License active '
                "and verified</code>, open your web browser and navigate to your server's secure WHM administration "
                'URL:</p>\n'
                '  <pre class="overflow-x-auto rounded-xl bg-navy p-4 text-sm leading-relaxed '
                'text-gray-100"><code>https://YOUR-SERVER-IP:2087</code></pre>\n'
                '  <p>Log in with username <code class="rounded bg-mist px-1.5 py-0.5 text-[0.85em] '
                'text-navy">root</code> and your server\'s root password to access the initial WHM setup wizard and '
                'configure nameservers, contact email, and default PHP versions.</p>\n'
                '</section>\n'
                '\n'
                '<section class="space-y-4">\n'
                '  <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-navy">5. Initial WHM Security and '
                'Performance Hardening</h2>\n'
                '  <p>After completing the activation wizard, execute these baseline server hardening '
                'configurations:</p>\n'
                '  <ul class="list-disc space-y-2 pl-6">\n'
