                '    <code># Check if LiteSpeed is actively listening on ports 80/443<br>netstat -tulpn | grep '
                'lshttpd<br><br># Check LiteSpeed runtime status<br>/usr/local/lsws/bin/lswsctrl status<br><br># If '
                'port conflict occurs with stale Apache processes<br>killall -9 httpd<br>/usr/local/lsws/bin/lswsctrl '
                'restart</code>\n'
                '  </div>\n'
                '  <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">Enjoy enterprise performance and seamless management with '
                'an affordable <a href="/litespeed-license" class="text-brand-600 hover:text-brand-700 underline '
                'font-medium">LiteSpeed license</a> from LicenBase.</p>\n'
                '</section>\n'
                '\n'
                '\n'
                '<section class="space-y-4">\n'
                '  <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-8 mb-4 tracking-tight">Summary: Verification '
                'Commands After Installation</h2>\n'
                '  <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">Once your installation and traffic switch are complete, '
                'verify all subsystems with these quick terminal commands:</p>\n'
                '  <div class="bg-gray-900 text-gray-100 p-4 rounded-xl font-mono text-sm overflow-x-auto my-4">\n'
                '    <code># Check LiteSpeed HTTP/HTTPS listeners<br>netstat -lnp | grep -E "(:80|:443)"<br><br># '
                'Check PHP LSAPI build and active modules<br>/usr/local/lsws/fcgi-bin/lsphp82 -m<br><br># Verify '
                'LSCache response header via curl<br>curl -I https://yourdomain.com | grep -i '
                '"x-litespeed-cache"</code>\n'
                '  </div>\n'
                '  <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">If the response header displays <code class="bg-gray-100 '
                'px-2 py-0.5 rounded text-sm text-gray-800">X-LiteSpeed-Cache: hit</code>, your server is delivering '
                'edge-cached pages directly from memory in under 40 milliseconds.</p>\n'
