                'py-0.5 text-[0.85em] text-navy">/usr/local/lsws/logs/error.log</code> typically reveals one of the '
                'following diagnostic messages:</p>\n'
                '  <ul class="list-disc space-y-2 pl-6">\n'
                '    <li><strong>[ERROR] License key is invalid or corrupted:</strong> Indicates the local <code '
                'class="rounded bg-mist px-1.5 py-0.5 text-[0.85em] text-navy">license.key</code> file is empty, '
                'expired, or has a mismatched hardware signature.</li>\n'
                '    <li><strong>[ERROR] Failed to contact license server:</strong> Indicates the server cannot '
                'establish an outbound TCP connection to the licensing gateway over port 443.</li>\n'
                '    <li><strong>[ERROR] Trial license expired:</strong> Indicates a temporary trial key has run its '
                'course and the server must be bound to a permanent automated IP license.</li>\n'
                '    <li><strong>[ERROR] Memory limit exceeded for license tier:</strong> Occurs if an entry-level '
                'license is installed on a server with more RAM than permitted by that tier.</li>\n'
                '  </ul>\n'
