                'Check active LiteSpeed version, license serial, and expiration\n'
                '/usr/local/lsws/bin/lshttpd -V</code></pre>\n'
                '  <p>Review the output to see your active serial number, maximum worker count, and license expiration '
                'timestamp. If the output indicates expired status, proceed to network testing.</p>\n'
                '</section>\n'
                '\n'
                '<section class="space-y-4">\n'
                '  <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-navy">Step 2: Test Network '
                'Connectivity to Licensing Gateway</h2>\n'
                '  <p>LiteSpeed requires outbound HTTPS access to its licensing cluster to periodically refresh signed '
                'certificates. Test outbound connectivity:</p>\n'
                '  <pre class="overflow-x-auto rounded-xl bg-navy p-4 text-sm leading-relaxed '
                'text-gray-100"><code>curl -Iv https://license.litespeedtech.com</code></pre>\n'
                '  <p>If the connection hangs or returns a timeout, check your firewall configuration (such as '
                'ConfigServer Security &amp; Firewall - CSF):</p>\n'
                '  <pre class="overflow-x-auto rounded-xl bg-navy p-4 text-sm leading-relaxed text-gray-100"><code># '
                'In /etc/csf/csf.conf, ensure TCP_OUT includes port 443\n'
                '# Then reload CSF:\n'
                'csf -r</code></pre>\n'
                '</section>\n'
                '\n'
                '<section class="space-y-4">\n'
                '  <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-navy">Step 3: Force License '
                'Re-Verification and Key Refresh</h2>\n'
                '  <p>To force LiteSpeed to download a fresh cryptographic key file and verify your IP address with '
                'LicenBase, execute:</p>\n'
                '  <pre class="overflow-x-auto rounded-xl bg-navy p-4 text-sm leading-relaxed text-gray-100"><code># '
                'Force license update\n'
                '/usr/local/lsws/bin/lshttpd -r\n'
                '\n'
                '# Restart LiteSpeed gracefully\n'
                'systemctl restart lsws</code></pre>\n'
                '  <p>If you manage LiteSpeed inside cPanel &amp; WHM, you can also navigate to <strong>WHM &gt; '
                'Plugins &gt; LiteSpeed Web Server Plugin &gt; Version Management</strong> and trigger a graceful '
                'restart.</p>\n'
                '</section>\n'
                '\n'
