                'multi-tenant web hosting environments:</p>\n'
                '  <ul class="list-disc space-y-2 pl-6">\n'
                '    <li><strong>Lightweight Virtualized Environments (LVE):</strong> Enforces strict per-user limits '
                'on CPU percentage, memory allocation (RAM), disk I/O throughput (IOPS), and entry processes '
                '(concurrent HTTP connections).</li>\n'
                '    <li><strong>CageFS Virtualized File System:</strong> Encloses each cPanel account inside its own '
                "private virtual filesystem jail. Users cannot view system configuration files, other users' home "
                'directories, or running system daemons.</li>\n'
                '    <li><strong>MySQL Governor:</strong> Monitors database usage in real time and automatically '
                'throttles slow or abusive queries before they exhaust database server connections.</li>\n'
                '    <li><strong>HardenedPHP:</strong> Backports critical security patches to legacy PHP versions '
                '(such as PHP 7.4, 7.3, and 5.6), allowing you to run older client applications securely without '
                'exposing the server to known CVE vulnerabilities.</li>\n'
                '    <li><strong>PHP / NodeJS / Python Selector:</strong> Allows end users to select their preferred '
                'runtime version and enable required extensions directly within their cPanel dashboard.</li>\n'
                '  </ul>\n'
                '</section>\n'
                '\n'
                '<section class="space-y-4">\n'
                '  <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-navy">MySQL Governor: Real-Time '
                'Database Throttling</h2>\n'
                '  <p>Unindexed MySQL database queries are the number one cause of server crashes in shared cPanel '
                'environments. Standard Linux cannot attribute MySQL queries to individual Linux user accounts because '
                'all queries execute through the central <code class="rounded bg-mist px-1.5 py-0.5 text-[0.85em] '
                'text-navy">mysqld</code> daemon. CloudLinux MySQL Governor tracks CPU and I/O consumption per cPanel '
                'account in real time:</p>\n'
                '  <pre class="overflow-x-auto rounded-xl bg-navy p-4 text-sm leading-relaxed text-gray-100"><code># '
                'View real-time database usage by cPanel user\n'
                'dbctl --list\n'
                '\n'
                '# Configure governor mode to automatic throttling\n'
                'dbctl --set-mode=auto</code></pre>\n'
                '  <p>When an account exceeds its allocated database throttle limits, MySQL Governor pauses that '
                "user's queries for several milliseconds, preventing server-wide database lockups while keeping the "
                'site reachable.</p>\n'
                '</section>\n'
                '\n'
                '<section class="space-y-4">\n'
