                'metric telemetry, LLM log vector analysis, and automated remediation triggers.</figcaption>\n'
                '</figure>\n'
                '\n'
                '<section class="space-y-4">\n'
                '  <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-8 mb-3">1. Moving Beyond Static Threshold Alerting '
                'to Predictive ML</h2>\n'
                '  <p class="text-gray-600">Static monitoring rules (e.g. <em>"alert if RAM &gt; 85%"</em>) produce '
                'constant false alarms during routine nightly backups or fail to catch slow memory leaks until the '
                'Linux Out-Of-Memory (OOM) killer terminates the MariaDB database daemon. AI monitoring continuously '
                'analyzes historical workload baselines, learning diurnal traffic curves and distinguishing between '
                'scheduled administrative cron jobs and dangerous resource spikes.</p>\n'
                '  <p class="text-gray-600">By modeling time-series telemetry through lightweight machine learning '
                'algorithms (such as isolation forests and Holt-Winters seasonal decomposition), AI tools can alert '
                'administrators 40 to 90 minutes before an impending server outage occurs.</p>\n'
                '</section>\n'
                '\n'
                '<section class="space-y-4">\n'
                '  <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-8 mb-3">2. Automated Log Vector Analysis and Threat '
                'Detection</h2>\n'
                '  <p class="text-gray-600">Modern web hosting servers generate millions of log lines daily across '
                '<code>/var/log/messages</code>, Apache/LiteSpeed access logs, and Exim mail queues. AI models ingest '
                'these continuous log streams, vectorizing unstructured text to identify subtle threat '
                'signatures:</p>\n'
                '  <ul class="list-disc pl-5 text-gray-600 space-y-2">\n'
                '    <li><strong>Distributed Brute-Force SSH Attacks:</strong> Detecting dictionary attacks '
                'coordinated across thousands of rotating residential IP addresses where each individual IP only '
                'attempts 1 login per hour.</li>\n'
                '    <li><strong>Slow HTTP Application Exhaustion:</strong> Identifying Slowloris and slow POST '
                'requests that slowly exhaust web server worker threads without generating noticeable network '
                'bandwidth spikes.</li>\n'
                '    <li><strong>Compromised CMS Account Activity:</strong> Flagging suspicious PHP execution chains, '
                'unauthorized base64 eval functions, and anomalous spikes in outbound email queues.</li>\n'
                '  </ul>\n'
                '</section>\n'
                '\n'
                '<section class="space-y-4">\n'
                '  <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-8 mb-3">3. Autonomous Remediation Pipelines and '
                'Self-Healing Daemons</h2>\n'
                '  <p class="text-gray-600">When an AI monitoring agent detects abnormal latency spikes or PHP worker '
                'deadlocks, it does not merely send an alert—it executes automated, pre-approved healing routines to '
                'prevent downtime:</p>\n'
                '  <ul class="list-disc pl-5 text-gray-600 space-y-2">\n'
                '    <li>Gracefully reloading PHP-FPM or LiteSpeed worker daemons to reclaim leaked virtual '
                'memory.</li>\n'
                '    <li>Injecting temporary CSF firewall blocks against abusive IP subnets exhibiting coordinated '
                'scraping behavior.</li>\n'
                '    <li>Killing stuck, unindexed MariaDB queries that have been holding table locks for longer than '
                '60 seconds.</li>\n'
                '  </ul>\n'
                '</section>\n'
                '\n'
                '<section class="space-y-4">\n'
                '  <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-8 mb-3">4. Lightweight Edge Telemetry on Budget VPS '
                'Hardware</h2>\n'
                '  <p class="text-gray-600">A common misconception is that AI monitoring requires massive CPU and GPU '
                'resources on the monitored server. In reality, modern edge agents (such as Netdata ML and Vector by '
                'Datadog) sample system metrics every second using less than 1% vCPU and under 40 MB of RAM.</p>\n'
                '  <p class="text-gray-600">Heavyweight vector embedding computations and LLM anomaly reasoning are '
                'offloaded asynchronously to centralized monitoring clusters or external API endpoints, ensuring zero '
                'performance penalty on client websites. This hybrid edge-cloud architecture guarantees that your live '
                'WordPress sites and MariaDB database transactions maintain peak responsiveness even during intensive '
                'log analysis sweeps.</p>\n'
                '</section>\n'
                '\n'
                '<section class="space-y-4">\n'
                '  <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-8 mb-3">5. Summary: Build Self-Healing '
                'Infrastructure with Wholesale Licensing</h2>\n'
