                '</section>\n'
                '\n'
                '<section class="space-y-4">\n'
                '  <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-8 mb-3">3. Audit and Purge Stale, Dormant, and '
                'Suspended Accounts</h2>\n'
                "  <p>Many system administrators do not realize that cPanel's licensing mechanism counts <em>every "
                'single user account</em> located in <code>/var/cpanel/users</code>. If a client failed to pay an '
                'invoice six months ago and you simply suspended their account in WHM, that dead account still counts '
                'toward your license threshold, potentially pushing you into a higher pricing tier.</p>\n'
                '  <p>Conduct a monthly hygiene routine to archive and remove dormant accounts:</p>\n'
                '  <pre class="overflow-x-auto rounded-xl bg-gray-900 p-4 text-sm text-gray-100 font-mono"><code># '
                'List suspended accounts and check creation dates\n'
                'whmapi1 list_suspended\n'
                '\n'
                '# Backup dormant accounts to remote storage before termination\n'
                '/scripts/pkgacct username /backup/remote_staging/\n'
                '\n'
                '# Terminate unneeded user accounts to reclaim license slots\n'
                'whmapi1 removeacct user=username</code></pre>\n'
                '  <p>By automating the removal of non-paying or former clients, you keep your active count strictly '
                'within lower tier limits like Admin (up to 5 accounts) or Pro (up to 30 accounts).</p>\n'
                '</section>\n'
                '\n'
                '<section class="space-y-4">\n'
                '  <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-8 mb-3">4. Consolidate Low-Traffic Sites Under Addon '
                'Domains</h2>\n'
                '  <p>If you manage multiple internal projects, staging environments, personal blogs, or micro-sites '
                'for a single client, creating a separate cPanel account for each one wastes licensed account slots. '
                "In cPanel's licensing logic, one cPanel account can host unlimited addon domains, subdomains, and "
                'databases without consuming extra license quotas.</p>\n'
                '  <p>Consolidating five low-traffic websites into a single cPanel account under addon domains reduces '
                'five licensed accounts down to one. For digital agencies managing 20 or 30 static client websites, '
                'this single architectural shift can drop your required license tier from cPanel Pro down to cPanel '
                'Admin, generating hundreds of dollars in annual savings.</p>\n'
                '</section>\n'
                '\n'
                '<section class="space-y-4">\n'
                '  <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-8 mb-3">5. Boost Tenant Density with LiteSpeed Web '
                'Server</h2>\n'
                '  <p>When shared servers run standard Apache web servers, high PHP resource consumption frequently '
