                '</section>\n'
                '\n'
                '<section class="space-y-4">\n'
                '  <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-8 mb-3">6. Stabilize Noisy Tenants with CloudLinux '
                'LVE Limits</h2>\n'
                '  <p>Unruly or infected websites that exhaust CPU and RAM often force hosting teams to migrate '
                'accounts across multiple nodes to maintain stability. Deploying a <a href="/cloudlinux-license" '
                'class="text-blue-600 font-semibold hover:underline">CloudLinux license</a> implements kernel-level '
                'Lightweight Virtual Environment (LVE) isolation.</p>\n'
                '  <p>With CloudLinux, every cPanel user receives explicit CPU, RAM, and disk I/O caps. A traffic '
                'spike on one website will never bring down neighboring sites. This strict resource fence lets you '
                'safely push server capacity to its maximum safe threshold, avoiding the need for redundant cluster '
                'infrastructure.</p>\n'
                '</section>\n'
                '\n'
                '<section class="space-y-4">\n'
                '  <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-8 mb-3">7. Take Advantage of Multi-License Bundle '
                'Deals</h2>\n'
                '  <p>Licensing individual server components from separate vendors creates billing fragmentation and '
                'missed bulk discount opportunities. Top hosting companies stack their core software together through '
                'unified suppliers.</p>\n'
                '  <p>By purchasing discounted software stacks through our <a href="/deals" class="text-blue-600 '
                'font-semibold hover:underline">combo discount bundles</a>, you can acquire cPanel, LiteSpeed, and '
