                'campaign tracking parameters feeding into web analytics.</figcaption>\n'
                '  </figure>\n'
                '</section>\n'
                '\n'
                '<section class="space-y-4">\n'
                '  <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-8 mb-3">2. Best Practices for Bulletproof UTM '
                'Governance</h2>\n'
                '  <p>Messy UTM tagging creates fragmented analytics dashboards. Adhere to these essential naming '
                'rules:</p>\n'
                '  <ol class="list-decimal space-y-2 pl-6">\n'
                '    <li><strong>Strictly Use Lowercase:</strong> Because GA4 treats <code>Email</code> and '
                '<code>email</code> as two separate medium classifications, enforce lowercase across all '
                'parameters.</li>\n'
                '    <li><strong>Use Hyphens Instead of Spaces:</strong> Never use spaces or underscores in parameter '
                'values. Spaces become encoded as messy <code>%20</code> strings in browsers. Use hyphens (e.g., '
                '<code>summer-sale</code>).</li>\n'
                '    <li><strong>Never Tag Internal Links:</strong> Appending UTM tags to internal website links '
                "resets the visitor's session origin, destroying your conversion tracking and inflating bounce "
                'rates.</li>\n'
                '    <li><strong>Maintain Self-Referencing Canonical Tags:</strong> Always ensure every landing page '
                'specifies its clean URL in its <code>&lt;link rel="canonical"&gt;</code> tag to protect your SEO '
                'rankings from duplicate content penalties.</li>\n'
                '  </ol>\n'
                '</section>\n'
                '\n'
                '<section class="space-y-4">\n'
                '  <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-8 mb-3">3. Tracking Hosting Conversions in WHMCS and '
