                'transfer volumes, peak throughput, and CDN offloading.</figcaption>\n'
                '  </figure>\n'
                '</section>\n'
                '\n'
                '<section class="space-y-4">\n'
                '  <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-8 mb-3">2. 95th Percentile Billing vs Flat Quota '
                'Caps</h2>\n'
                '  <p>Enterprise data centers frequently bill colocation and dedicated servers using 95th percentile '
                'metrics:</p>\n'
                '  <p>By discarding the top 5% of temporary spike intervals (roughly 36 hours over a 30-day billing '
                'cycle), providers allow you to absorb brief DDoS attacks or marketing traffic surges without billing '
                'you at peak port rates. However, if your daily sustained traffic regularly saturates 80% of your '
                'uplink, your 95th percentile billing tier will jump substantially. Learn how to plan retail plan '
                'pricing around bandwidth margins in our <a '
                'href="/blog/hosting-break-even-calculator-pricing-strategy" class="text-blue-600 font-semibold '
                'hover:underline">Hosting Break-Even &amp; Pricing Calculator Guide</a>.</p>\n'
                '</section>\n'
                '\n'
                '<section class="space-y-4">\n'
                '  <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-8 mb-3">3. Offloading Bandwidth with LiteSpeed '
                'Compression</h2>\n'
                '  <p>Deploying <a href="/litespeed-license" class="text-blue-600 font-semibold '
                'hover:underline">LiteSpeed Web Server</a> provides out-of-the-box Brotli compression and HTTP/3 QUIC '
                'stream multiplexing. By compressing static HTML, CSS, JavaScript, and SVG assets on the fly, '
