                '<p class="text-lg text-gray-600">On a cPanel &amp; WHM hosting server, the <strong>Exim Mail Transfer '
                'Agent (MTA)</strong> handles thousands of inbound and outbound transactions daily. However, when the '
                'mail queue gets stuck—accumulating thousands of deferred or frozen messages—legitimate customer '
                'emails stop delivering, server load spikes, and upstream mail providers (like Gmail, Outlook, and '
                "Yahoo) begin throttling or blacklisting your server's IP address. Resolving a bloated Exim queue "
                'requires surgical triage: you must flush legitimate customer communications while identifying and '
                'deleting malicious spam runs without destroying real data. This guide provides an actionable '
                'troubleshooting playbook for system administrators to diagnose, clean, and unfreeze a stuck Exim '
                'queue on a <a href="/cpanel-license" class="text-blue-600 font-semibold hover:underline">cPanel '
                'server</a>.</p>\n'
                '\n'
                '<section class="space-y-4">\n'
                '  <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-8 mb-3">Exim Queue Message States: Active, Deferred, '
                'and Frozen</h2>\n'
                '  <p>To troubleshoot queue delays effectively, administrators must distinguish between the three '
                'primary states Exim assigns to queued messages:</p>\n'
                '  <figure class="my-6 rounded-xl overflow-hidden border border-gray-200 bg-gray-900/5 p-2">\n'
                '  <img src="/assets/img/blog/troubleshoot-stuck-exim-mail-queue-whm-1.svg" alt="Exim MTA mail queue '
                'processing stages and troubleshooting diagram on cPanel" width="800" height="420" class="w-full '
                'h-auto rounded-lg shadow-sm" loading="lazy">\n'
                '  <figcaption class="text-xs text-gray-500 text-center mt-2 px-2">Figure 1: Exim message lifecycle '
                'stages, retry delays, and administrative command playbook.</figcaption>\n'
                '</figure>\n'
                '  <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2 text-gray-700">\n'
                '    <li><strong>Active / Pending:</strong> Freshly submitted messages waiting for DNS lookups or '
                'remote SMTP socket handshakes. In healthy servers, messages remain in this state for only a few '
                'seconds.</li>\n'
                '    <li><strong>Deferred (Retry Delay):</strong> Delivery was attempted, but the destination server '
                'returned a temporary failure (4xx response), such as <code>451 Greylisted</code> or <code>421 Too '
                'many concurrent connections</code>. Exim records the failure in its internal retry database '
                '(<code>/var/spool/exim/db/retry</code>) and calculates exponential retry intervals.</li>\n'
                '    <li><strong>Frozen (<code>*** frozen ***</code>):</strong> Delivery failed permanently, and '
                "Exim's attempt to return a bounce message to the sender address was also rejected (a classic "
                'signature of outbound spam generated with forged sender headers). Exim halts automated processing on '
                'frozen emails to prevent mail loops.</li>\n'
                '  </ul>\n'
                '</section>\n'
                '\n'
                '<section class="space-y-4">\n'
                '  <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-8 mb-3">Step 1: Check Queue Size and Identify Top '
                'Senders</h2>\n'
                '  <p>Begin by logging into your server via SSH as <code>root</code> to determine the scale of the '
                'queue backlog:</p>\n'
                '  <div class="bg-gray-900 rounded-lg p-4 font-mono text-xs text-gray-100 overflow-x-auto">\n'
                '    <p class="text-gray-400"># Count total queued messages</p>\n'
                '    <p>exim -bpc</p>\n'
                '    <p class="text-gray-400 mt-2"># Display summary breakdown of senders and recipients using '
                'eximst</p>\n'
                '    <p>exim -bp | exiqsumm</p>\n'
                '  </div>\n'
                '  <p>The <code>exiqsumm</code> output organizes queued messages by domain, volume, and oldest message '
                'age. If a single domain accounts for 8,000 out of 8,500 messages, that domain is either executing a '
                'massive newsletter campaign or has been compromised by a spammer.</p>\n'
                '</section>\n'
                '\n'
                '<section class="space-y-4">\n'
                '  <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-8 mb-3">Step 2: Inspect Individual Queued Messages '
                'Without Deletion</h2>\n'
                '  <p>Before purging any email, inspect a sample message to verify whether it is legitimate business '
                'communication or malicious spam. Pick a message ID from <code>exim -bp</code> and inspect its '
                'components:</p>\n'
                '  <div class="bg-gray-900 rounded-lg p-4 font-mono text-xs text-gray-100 overflow-x-auto">\n'
                '    <p class="text-gray-400"># View message headers (reveals authenticated sender and originating '
                'script)</p>\n'
                '    <p>exim -Mvh 1t8Zab-0001bc-2d</p>\n'
                '    <p class="text-gray-400 mt-2"># View message body text</p>\n'
                '    <p>exim -Mvb 1t8Zab-0001bc-2d</p>\n'
                '    <p class="text-gray-400 mt-2"># View delivery transaction log (shows exact SMTP rejection '
                'response)</p>\n'
                '    <p>exim -Mvl 1t8Zab-0001bc-2d</p>\n'
                '  </div>\n'
                '  <p>In the headers (<code>-Mvh</code>), examine the <code>X-PHP-Script</code> or '
                '<code>X-Authenticated-Sender</code> lines. If an infected WordPress plugin is pumping spam through '
                'PHP <code>mail()</code>, this header will point directly to the exact file path (e.g., '
                '<code>/home/user/public_html/wp-content/uploads/cache.php</code>). If the spam originates from an '
                'authenticated mailbox, suspend that specific email user in cPanel immediately.</p>\n'
                '</section>\n'
                '\n'
                '<section class="space-y-4">\n'
                '  <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-8 mb-3">Step 3: Safely Flushing Legitimate '
                'Messages</h2>\n'
                '  <p>If the queue accumulated because of a temporary network outage or firewall glitch that is now '
                'resolved, you can trigger an immediate delivery run for all legitimate pending messages:</p>\n'
                '  <div class="bg-gray-900 rounded-lg p-4 font-mono text-xs text-gray-100 overflow-x-auto">\n'
                '    <p class="text-gray-400"># Force delivery run of pending queue</p>\n'
                '    <p>exim -qf</p>\n'
                '    <p class="text-gray-400 mt-2"># Force queue run ignoring retry delays (processes greylisted '
                'messages immediately)</p>\n'
                '    <p>exim -qff</p>\n'
                '  </div>\n'
                '  <p>To flush messages destined for a specific domain (for example, if Gmail unblocked your IP and '
                'you want to deliver queued Google Workspace messages):</p>\n'
                '  <div class="bg-gray-900 rounded-lg p-4 font-mono text-xs text-gray-100 overflow-x-auto">\n'
                '    <p>exim -R gmail.com</p>\n'
                '  </div>\n'
                '</section>\n'
                '\n'
                '<section class="space-y-4">\n'
                '  <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-8 mb-3">Step 4: Purging Frozen Spam and Malicious '
                'Backlogs</h2>\n'
                '  <p>Frozen messages consume disk space and inode allocations in <code>/var/spool/exim/input/</code> '
                'while slowing down queue processing. You can safely purge all frozen messages in bulk without '
                'touching active, legitimate emails:</p>\n'
                '  <div class="bg-gray-900 rounded-lg p-4 font-mono text-xs text-gray-100 overflow-x-auto">\n'
                '    <p class="text-gray-400"># Delete all frozen messages from queue</p>\n'
                '    <p>exiqgrep -z -i | xargs exim -Mrm</p>\n'
