                '<p class="text-lg text-gray-600">As cPanel\'s per-account licensing costs have grown, many web '
                'hosting providers, agencies, and VPS owners have chosen to migrate their infrastructure to '
                '<strong>DirectAdmin</strong>. DirectAdmin offers a lightweight, modern, and cost-effective hosting '
                'control panel with native support for OpenLiteSpeed, Nginx, and Apache. However, migrating production '
                'websites—along with MySQL databases, mailboxes, DNS zones, and SSL certificates—requires a '
                'meticulous, structured process to avoid data loss. This guide details the complete migration playbook '
                'from <a href="/cpanel-license" class="text-blue-600 font-semibold hover:underline">cPanel</a> to '
                'DirectAdmin, ensuring zero downtime and complete data integrity.</p>\n'
                '\n'
                '<section class="space-y-4">\n'
                '  <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-8 mb-3">The Migration Pipeline: Overview and '
                'Strategy</h2>\n'
                '  <p>The cPanel-to-DirectAdmin migration workflow is divided into three sequential phases:</p>\n'
                '  <figure class="my-6 rounded-xl overflow-hidden border border-gray-200 bg-gray-900/5 p-2">\n'
                '  <img src="/assets/img/blog/migrate-cpanel-to-directadmin-without-data-loss-1.svg" alt="cPanel to '
                'DirectAdmin migration pipeline and automated conversion diagram" width="800" height="420" '
                'class="w-full h-auto rounded-lg shadow-sm" loading="lazy">\n'
                '  <figcaption class="text-xs text-gray-500 text-center mt-2 px-2">Figure 1: Complete data extraction, '
                'translation, and zero-downtime DNS cutover pipeline.</figcaption>\n'
                '</figure>\n'
                '  <ol class="list-decimal pl-6 space-y-2 text-gray-700">\n'
                '    <li><strong>Phase 1: Source Data Packaging:</strong> Generating clean <code>cpmove</code> '
                'archives on the cPanel server using native command-line packaging scripts.</li>\n'
                "    <li><strong>Phase 2: Archive Translation &amp; Restoration:</strong> Using DirectAdmin's native "
                'conversion scripts to translate cPanel configuration formats (like <code>public_html</code> paths, '
                'crontabs, and Maildir structures) into DirectAdmin user schemes.</li>\n'
                '    <li><strong>Phase 3: Final Sync &amp; DNS Cutover:</strong> Executing a final incremental delta '
                'synchronization of mail and databases, followed by switching authoritative DNS records.</li>\n'
                '  </ol>\n'
                '</section>\n'
                '\n'
                '<section class="space-y-4">\n'
                '  <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-8 mb-3">Step 1: Preparing and Packaging Accounts on '
                'cPanel</h2>\n'
                '  <p>Log into your source cPanel server via SSH as <code>root</code>. Ensure you lower DNS TTL values '
                'across all zones to <strong>300 seconds (5 minutes)</strong> at least 24 hours prior to cutover.</p>\n'
                '  <p>Generate full cPanel backups for your accounts:</p>\n'
                '  <div class="bg-gray-900 rounded-lg p-4 font-mono text-xs text-gray-100 overflow-x-auto">\n'
                '    <p class="text-gray-400"># Package a single account</p>\n'
                '    <p>/scripts/pkgacct username /home/cpmove-backups/</p>\n'
                '    <p class="text-gray-400 mt-2"># Or package all accounts in a batch loop:</p>\n'
                "    <p>for user in $(cat /etc/trueuserdomains | awk '{print $2}'); do /scripts/pkgacct $user "
                '/home/cpmove-backups/; done</p>\n'
                '  </div>\n'
                '  <p>Transfer the generated archives to the new DirectAdmin server via <code>rsync</code>:</p>\n'
                '  <div class="bg-gray-900 rounded-lg p-4 font-mono text-xs text-gray-100 overflow-x-auto">\n'
                '    <p class="text-gray-400"># Transfer directly to DirectAdmin import directory</p>\n'
                '    <p>rsync -avz -e "ssh -p 22" /home/cpmove-backups/cpmove-*.tar.gz '
                'root@da-server-ip:/home/admin/all_backups/</p>\n'
                '  </div>\n'
                '</section>\n'
                '\n'
                '<section class="space-y-4">\n'
                '  <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-8 mb-3">Step 2: Restoring Backups Inside '
                'DirectAdmin</h2>\n'
                '  <p>DirectAdmin includes built-in conversion capabilities that automatically parse cPanel '
                'tarballs.</p>\n'
                '  <ol class="list-decimal pl-6 space-y-2 text-gray-700">\n'
                '    <li>Log into the <strong>DirectAdmin Web Interface</strong> as <code>admin</code> at '
                '<code>https://your-da-server:2222</code>.</li>\n'
                '    <li>Navigate to <strong>Admin Tools &raquo; Admin Backup/Transfer</strong>.</li>\n'
                '    <li>Under the <strong>Restore</strong> tab, select the directory path where you transferred the '
                'files: <code>/home/admin/all_backups</code>.</li>\n'
                '    <li>DirectAdmin will automatically detect the <code>cpmove-*.tar.gz</code> naming convention and '
                'display the cPanel accounts.</li>\n'
                '    <li>Select the IP assignment (Shared Server IP or Dedicated IP) and click '
                '<strong>Restore</strong>.</li>\n'
                '  </ol>\n'
                '  <p>Alternatively, administrators who prefer the command line can trigger the conversion utility '
                'directly:</p>\n'
                '  <div class="bg-gray-900 rounded-lg p-4 font-mono text-xs text-gray-100 overflow-x-auto">\n'
                '    <p class="text-gray-400"># Run the native CLI conversion tool in DirectAdmin</p>\n'
                '    <p>/usr/local/directadmin/scripts/cpanel_to_da/cpanel_to_da.sh '
                '/home/admin/all_backups/cpmove-username.tar.gz</p>\n'
                '  </div>\n'
                '</section>\n'
                '\n'
                '<section class="space-y-4">\n'
                '  <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-8 mb-3">Step 3: Post-Migration Verification &amp; '
                'Delta Sync</h2>\n'
                '  <p>Before modifying DNS records, verify website rendering on the new server. You can simulate '
                "traffic locally by adding an entry to your workstation's <code>hosts</code> file (mapping the domain "
                'name directly to the DirectAdmin server IP).</p>\n'
                '  <p>Test WordPress database connectivity, check SSL certificates (which can be re-issued instantly '
                "via DirectAdmin's built-in Let's Encrypt manager), and test webmail access via Roundcube.</p>\n"
                '  <p>To capture any emails received on the old server while testing was underway, run a final delta '
                'rsync of the mail directories:</p>\n'
                '  <div class="bg-gray-900 rounded-lg p-4 font-mono text-xs text-gray-100 overflow-x-auto">\n'
                '    <p class="text-gray-400"># Sync any newly arrived emails prior to final DNS update</p>\n'
                '    <p>rsync -avz /home/username/mail/ root@da-server-ip:/home/username/imap/</p>\n'
                '  </div>\n'
                '  <p>Once verified, update your nameservers or A records to point to your new DirectAdmin server IP. '
                'Thanks to the 300-second TTL configured earlier, global propagation will complete in minutes.</p>\n'
                '</section>\n'
                '\n'
                '<section class="space-y-4">\n'
                '  <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-8 mb-3">Maximizing ROI on DirectAdmin</h2>\n'
                '  <p>Pairing DirectAdmin with high-performance software transforms your hosting infrastructure. You '
                'can run <a href="/litespeed-license" class="text-blue-600 font-semibold hover:underline">LiteSpeed '
                'Web Server</a> or OpenLiteSpeed natively inside DirectAdmin CustomBuild, cutting memory usage while '
                'serving content at lightning speed.</p>\n'
                '  <p>LicenBase provides automated, low-cost licensing solutions for hosting control panels, web '
                'servers, and backup tools. Whether you choose cPanel or DirectAdmin, our team ensures your server '
                'remains fully licensed, stable, and cost-optimized.</p>\n'
                '</section>\n',
