                '<p class="text-lg text-gray-600">When upgrading a web hosting server from Apache to an enterprise <a '
                'href="/litespeed-license" class="text-blue-600 font-semibold hover:underline">LiteSpeed Web Server '
                'license</a>, the most common architectural question administrators ask is: <strong>"How many '
                'LiteSpeed workers does my server actually need?"</strong> Because LiteSpeed\'s licensing '
                'tiers—Starter (1-Worker), Web Host Essential (1-Worker), Web Host Elite (2-Worker), and Web Host '
                'Enterprise (4+ Workers)—are tiered by worker count, choosing the right license directly impacts both '
                "monthly software expenditure and real-world throughput. This guide demystifies LiteSpeed's "
                'event-driven worker architecture and outlines how to size your server for peak performance.</p>\n'
                '\n'
                '<section class="space-y-4">\n'
                '  <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-8 mb-3">The Difference Between LSWS Workers and PHP '
                'Processes</h2>\n'
                '  <p>To avoid overpaying for unnecessary license tiers, you must understand what a LiteSpeed worker '
                'is—and what it is not.</p>\n'
                '  <figure class="my-6 rounded-xl overflow-hidden border border-gray-200 bg-gray-900/5 p-2">\n'
                '  <img src="/assets/img/blog/litespeed-worker-sizing-how-many-workers-vps-1.svg" alt="LiteSpeed Web '
                'Server worker process sizing and CPU core allocation diagram" width="800" height="420" class="w-full '
                'h-auto rounded-lg shadow-sm" loading="lazy">\n'
                '  <figcaption class="text-xs text-gray-500 text-center mt-2 px-2">Figure 1: LiteSpeed event-driven '
                'worker processes vs separate LSPHP dynamic worker pools.</figcaption>\n'
                '</figure>\n'
                "  <p>Unlike Apache's <code>prefork</code> MPM, which requires a dedicated worker process for every "
                'single concurrent visitor, LiteSpeed operates on an <strong>asynchronous, event-driven '
                'engine</strong> similar to Nginx. A single LiteSpeed worker can easily maintain <strong>10,000+ '
                'simultaneous keep-alive HTTP connections</strong> while consuming under 50 MB of RAM.</p>\n'
                '  <p>LiteSpeed workers handle:</p>\n'
                '  <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2 text-gray-700">\n'
                '    <li>Accepting incoming TCP sockets on ports 80 and 443.</li>\n'
                '    <li>Performing SSL/TLS cryptographic handshakes.</li>\n'
                '    <li>Serving static assets (images, CSS, JS) directly from disk or kernel page cache.</li>\n'
                '    <li>Serving full-page cached dynamic pages via LSCache without touching PHP or MySQL.</li>\n'
                '  </ul>\n'
                '  <p><strong>PHP Execution is Separate:</strong> Dynamic PHP scripts are executed by separate '
                '<strong>LSPHP worker processes</strong>. Your server can spawn 50 or 100 LSPHP processes to execute '
                'WordPress or WooCommerce queries regardless of whether you have a 1-worker or 4-worker LiteSpeed '
                'license.</p>\n'
                '</section>\n'
                '\n'
                '<section class="space-y-4">\n'
                '  <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-8 mb-3">Sizing by Server Hardware and Traffic '
                'Profile</h2>\n'
                '  <div class="overflow-x-auto rounded-xl border border-gray-200">\n'
                '    <table class="w-full min-w-[34rem] text-sm">\n'
                '      <thead>\n'
                '        <tr>\n'
                '          <th class="border-b border-gray-200 bg-gray-50 px-4 py-3 text-left font-bold '
                'text-gray-700">LiteSpeed Tier</th>\n'
                '          <th class="border-b border-gray-200 bg-gray-50 px-4 py-3 text-left font-bold '
                'text-gray-700">Worker Count</th>\n'
                '          <th class="border-b border-gray-200 bg-gray-50 px-4 py-3 text-left font-bold '
                'text-gray-700">Recommended Hardware</th>\n'
                '          <th class="border-b border-gray-200 bg-gray-50 px-4 py-3 text-left font-bold '
                'text-gray-700">Optimal Workload</th>\n'
                '        </tr>\n'
                '      </thead>\n'
                '      <tbody>\n'
                '        <tr>\n'
                '          <td class="border-b border-gray-100 px-4 py-3 font-semibold text-gray-900">Starter / '
                'Essential</td>\n'
                '          <td class="border-b border-gray-100 px-4 py-3">1 Worker</td>\n'
                '          <td class="border-b border-gray-100 px-4 py-3">1 - 2 vCPUs, up to 8GB RAM</td>\n'
                '          <td class="border-b border-gray-100 px-4 py-3">Small agency VPS, single e-commerce store, '
                '&lt; 50 websites</td>\n'
                '        </tr>\n'
                '        <tr>\n'
                '          <td class="border-b border-gray-100 px-4 py-3 font-semibold text-gray-900">Web Host '
                'Elite</td>\n'
                '          <td class="border-b border-gray-100 px-4 py-3">2 Workers</td>\n'
                '          <td class="border-b border-gray-100 px-4 py-3">4 - 8 vCPUs, 16GB - 32GB RAM</td>\n'
                '          <td class="border-b border-gray-100 px-4 py-3">Shared hosting VPS nodes, high-traffic '
                'WooCommerce, 50-250 accounts</td>\n'
                '        </tr>\n'
                '        <tr>\n'
                '          <td class="border-b border-gray-100 px-4 py-3 font-semibold text-gray-900">Web Host '
                'Enterprise</td>\n'
                '          <td class="border-b border-gray-100 px-4 py-3">4 Workers</td>\n'
                '          <td class="border-b border-gray-100 px-4 py-3">8 - 16 Cores, 32GB - 64GB RAM</td>\n'
                '          <td class="border-b border-gray-100 px-4 py-3">Heavy shared hosting bare-metal machines, '
                'major media publishers</td>\n'
                '        </tr>\n'
                '        <tr>\n'
